CAR SHOWROOM:
    Class Used: Car
    Methods:
        __init__(self, model, company, price) → initializes car details.
    show(self) → displays car details.
    Simulates a car showroom system.
    Allows entering multiple car details: model, company, price.
    Uses instance variables for storing car details.
    Demonstrates class variable for showroom name.
    Stores multiple cars in a list.
    Displays all cars and can calculate total value of inventory.
    Example of inventory management system in OOP.


FLIGHT BOOKING:
    Class Used: FlightBooking
    Methods:
        __init__(self, passenger, seat, fare) → initializes booking.
    show(self) → displays booking details.
    Implements a flight booking system.
    Takes passenger details: name, seat number, fare.
    Stores each booking as an object of FlightBooking.
    Displays booking details for all passengers.
    Handles multiple passengers using loops.
    Demonstrates object creation inside loops.
    Simulates a real-world airline booking system.

   
 GYM MEMBERSHIP:  
    Class Used: Member
    Methods:
        __init__(self, name, months, fee) → initializes member data.
    total_fee(self) → calculates total fee.
    show(self) → displays member details.
    Represents a gym membership management system.
    Takes inputs: member name, months, monthly fee.
    Calculates total membership fee for each member.
    Uses methods for calculation and display.
    Stores multiple members in a list.
    Demonstrates how OOP can be used for billing systems.
    Simulates real-world fitness membership software.


MOBILE RECHARGE:
    Class Used: Recharge
    Methods:
        __init__(self, number, plan, cost) → initializes recharge details.
    how(self) → displays recharge details.
    Simulates a mobile recharge system.
    Takes inputs: mobile number, recharge plan, cost.
    ach recharge stored as an object of Recharge.
    Demonstrates class attribute for provider name.
    Stores multiple recharges using a list.
    Shows how objects can represent transactions.
    Example of a telecom recharge system in OOP.


ONLINE COURSE:
    Class Used: Course
    Methods:
        __init__(self, title, instructor, price) → initializes course details.
    show(self) → displays course details.
    discount(price) → (static method) applies discount.
    Implements an online course management system.
    Takes inputs: course title, instructor, price.
    Stores multiple courses as objects of Course.
    Demonstrates static methods for price discounts.
    Displays all entered courses.
    Helps understand lists of objects in Python.
    Simulates real-world e-learning platforms like Udemy.